  "analytic_review_groups": [
    "General smooth real background and fixed smooth-volume L1 topology are explicit; no mass hypothesis enters Perron interpolation.",
    "Affine time additions have zero Hessian, positive affine reparametrizations are holomorphic, and convex combinations/maxima preserve the product current inequality.",
    "Smooth background gauge changes preserve the exact product current.",
    "Finite convex parameter fibers and a bounded-interval Kiselman infimum provide integrable domination and interior L1 continuity.",
    "Endpoint almost-everywhere subsequences give the chord inequality; quasi-psh almost-everywhere order upgrades it everywhere.",
    "Vanishing endpoint coefficients and upper semicontinuity give joint upper limits, including endpoint poles.",
    "Existence of an admissible family is distinct from L1 attainment of both endpoints.",
    "The regularized product supremum preserves the jointly upper semicontinuous chord bound, imaginary-translation invariance and noncollapsed slices.",
    "A single endpoint-attaining competitor supplies an L1 squeeze for the Perron envelope.",
    "Smaller-interval Perron replacements glue by joint endpoint upper bounds and cannot exceed the original maximal family.",
    "Two explicit affine barriers for ordinarily equivalent endpoints attain the endpoints and retain their common pole set/type.",
    "Convex secant monotonicity gives the uniform time-Lipschitz bound away from common poles, also at finite endpoints.",
    "A common lower potential for different types gives an envelope without claiming endpoint attainment.",
    "The Real z convention gives cross factors one-half and acceleration factor one-quarter in the Hermitian product matrix.",
    "The positive spatial block admits the Schur complement; determinant zero is equivalent to the smooth homogeneous product equation.",
    "The d/dc normalization gives df wedge dcf = i/(2pi) partial f wedge bar-partial f and the stated gradient contraction.",
    "Action differentiation includes the time variation of eta^n and the full spatial adjoint of f-squared T.",
    "The spatial product rule has the signed first-order torsion terms and half coefficient on f-squared ddc T; the f ddc f terms cancel.",
    "Compact strict positivity permits arbitrary small smooth endpoint-fixed variations and the fundamental variational implication.",
    "Kahler closedness removes all torsion terms, while a Gauduchon slice removes only the last term.",
    "Nonzero constant translations are chord-maximal Perron segments and solve the homogeneous product equation; L2 stationarity is exactly ddc eta^(n-1)=0.",
    "Dimension one and the existing threefold persistence counterexample retain their own Gauduchon regimes; no complete singularity metric is asserted.",
    "Normalized decreasing envelope fixed points have a noncollapsed cutoff value; an envelope ray separately requires Perron maximality, ordinary projection and exact slope.",
    "Forward transforms have exact supremum ct, decreasing U_t-ct and ordinary envelope phi by monotonicity and the regularized supremum.",
    "An integrable fixed test-curve lower barrier and the pointwise initial bound give initial L1 convergence.",
    "Finite Perron replacements retain the linear upper bound and alter each inverse transform by at most (b-a)(c-tau).",
    "Kiselman inverse transforms are noncollapsed, ordinarily equivalent to Gamma_tau and at most zero; envelope maximality forces equality.",
    "Half-line duality recovers the replaced ray at every point, including fibers identically minus infinity.",
    "Inverse rays have a decreasing normalized cutoff limit; slopes above the cutoff give identically minus-infinity transforms.",
    "The obstacle P(g+C,0) yields an affine competitor on every finite interval; time translation identifies the relevant Perron family.",
    "Varying interval length before relative time tends to zero removes C and proves the inverse envelope fixed point.",
    "Pointwise initial limits are identified almost everywhere by L1 convergence, and half-line endpoint duality recovers the regularized initial potential.",
    "The cutoff infima commute, and closed-fiber duality gives the bijection with the stipulated cutoff convention.",
    "The Fubini-Study form has unit area; the logarithmic potential is smooth at infinity and has the normalized unit pole at zero.",
    "Tangent matching makes the radial convex potential C1 across its boundary; the full competitor maximum principle proves its ordinary envelope identity.",
    "Parameter concavity includes the zero and infinity fibers and negative parameters; the explicit optimizing lambda yields the smooth ray in both charts.",
    "Omitting nonpositive parameters incorrectly creates a pole in the ray at zero, while every finite ray slice is bounded.",
    "All six 151-point plot series match the stated analytic formulas within five-decimal rounding; axis labels, caption and concave/convex shapes are inspected."
